Look up shaderc and SPIRV-Cross by the names their static builds publish.

mpv's D3D11 renderer needs shaderc (GLSL to SPIR-V) and SPIRV-Cross (SPIR-V to
HLSL), and it looks for them as pkg-config `shaderc` and `spirv-cross-c-shared`.
Both of those names describe the shared-library variants:

  shaderc installs shaderc.pc (-lshaderc_shared), shaderc_static.pc and
  shaderc_combined.pc (-lshaderc_combined, one archive that already contains
  glslang and SPIRV-Tools).

  SPIRV-Cross installs spirv-cross-c.pc under SPIRV_CROSS_STATIC and
  spirv-cross-c-shared.pc under SPIRV_CROSS_SHARED. They are separate options
  and the static one does not publish the shared name.

The empv Windows runtime is a single self-contained libmpv-2.dll: everything is
linked in so the DLL imports nothing but Windows itself, which is what makes it
loadable from wherever the addon happens to be installed. Building the shared
variants instead would add two DLLs that would have to travel alongside it.

So this changes which pkg-config names mpv asks for, and nothing else. The
alternative was to install our own shaderc.pc and spirv-cross-c-shared.pc
pointing at the static archives, which would leave the build prefix asserting
that shared libraries exist when they do not -- a lie told to every other
consumer of that prefix in order to avoid editing two lines here.

Removal condition: drop this patch if mpv ever accepts the static pkg-config
names on its own (upstream `dependency(['shaderc', 'shaderc_combined'])` or
equivalent), or if the empv Windows runtime stops linking statically.

Applies to: mpv 0.41.0. Applied for the win32 build only -- these dependencies
exist solely for the D3D11 renderer, which mpv gates behind win32-desktop.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -995,7 +995,7 @@
     dependencies += sdl2
 endif

-shaderc = dependency('shaderc', required:
+shaderc = dependency('shaderc_combined', required:
     get_option('shaderc').require(features['win32-desktop']))
 features += {'shaderc': shaderc.found()}
 if features['shaderc']
@@ -1015,7 +1015,7 @@
     features += {'posix-shm': cc.has_function('shm_open', prefix: '#include <sys/mman.h>')}
 endif

-spirv_cross = dependency('spirv-cross-c-shared', required:
+spirv_cross = dependency('spirv-cross-c', required:
     get_option('spirv-cross').require(features['win32-desktop']))
 features += {'spirv-cross': spirv_cross.found()}
 if features['spirv-cross']
